ompressions  and i i'm across the hall from where  this has taken place but i knew it was  her  without even seeing i knew it was her  lear was pronounced dead inside the  hospital her cause of death hyperthermia  the unfortunate reality was we had spent  so much time on  risk assessing protect veterans protect  staff  and after that incident occurred we had  to take a step back and say well  there's a secondary risk too because of  the weather out here william caron is  the head of v.a southern nevada health  care system a policy is a policy  but with the heat and this was an  elderly woman  with a limp with her own health issues  she wasn't a veteran  but do you think a mistake was made at  the people who interacted with her at  the door  yeah i think we could go back in time  hindsight and  review every single detail but to say  that someone was was malicious or  reckless i wouldn't say that in the  least the the goal  was the greater good of protecting all  veterans  multiple departments at the v.a  investigated the incident the i-team's  request for the results of the  investigations were denied while we've  appealed we also asked karen about this  but any of those results of the  investigation typically that's not  something that we would share  outright were you aware that there was  further investigation no  it's the first time  that  i'm hearing this karen says policy was  changed the day lear died to allow one  visitor to accompany a patient and to  increase patrols in the parking lot were  you aware that they changed policy after  that  no  it will help someone else if it gets if  the same situation arises but it's not  helping me at all david says for now  he's trying to get used to life without  his wife of 57 years by his side i know  it's going to take time vanessa murphy  live local now  there are still unanswered questions  surrounding lear lit's death the va  first received the i-team's formal  request for information on the first of  february  now three months later the va has not  fulfilled that request

